data.content:
Output matches what you expected. Here's the full program:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var person = new Person("Jane", 30);
var options = new JsonSerializerOptions { PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase };
Console.WriteLine(JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options));

public record Person(string Name, int Age);
```

The key is `JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase` — it converts PascalCase properties (`Name`, `Age`) to camelCase (`name`, `age`) during serialization. No extra NuGet packages needed; `System.Text.Json` is built into .NET 8.
